@startuml MassagePaw_FSM
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName Monospace
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam shadowing false

title MassagePaw — State Machine Diagram (SysMLv2)\nstate def RobotHandFSM  ·  transitions: accept <Event> then <state>

' SysMLv2 state machine notation:
'   entry; then <state>          initial pseudo-state
'   accept <Event> then <state>  transition (replaces SysMLv1 "transition to X on Y")
'   entry action <action>        entry behavior
'   do    action <action>        do behavior

[*] --> idle : entry;\nthen idle

state idle {
  idle : entry action holdPosition\n      {HoldPosition}
}

state calibrating {
  calibrating : entry action runCalibration\n              {RunCalibration}
}

state teleopActive {
  teleopActive : entry action enableControl
  teleopActive : do    action executeCommand\n              {ExecuteTeleOpCommand:\n               applyForceScale →\n               solveIK →\n               runPIDControl}
}

state safetyHold {
  safetyHold : entry action freezeMotion\n             {FreezeMotion}
}

state emergencyStop {
  emergencyStop : entry action retractHand\n               {RetractHand — park pose,\n                cut motor torque}
}

' ── Transitions (SysMLv2: accept <occurrence> then <state>) ───────────────
idle           --> calibrating    : accept CalibrateCmd
calibrating    --> teleopActive   : accept CalibrationComplete
calibrating    --> idle           : accept CalibrationFailed

teleopActive   --> safetyHold     : accept ForceThresholdExceeded\n[contactForce > 5 N  REQ-002]
teleopActive   --> emergencyStop  : accept WatchdogTimeout\n[no cmd > 100 ms  REQ-005]
teleopActive   --> emergencyStop  : accept EStopSignal
teleopActive   --> idle           : accept DisconnectCmd

safetyHold     --> teleopActive   : accept OperatorAcknowledge
safetyHold     --> emergencyStop  : accept EStopSignal

emergencyStop  --> idle           : accept SystemReset

note right of teleopActive
  <b>occurrence def events</b>
  (SysMLv2 v2 replaces
  SysMLv1 SignalEvent):
  · ForceThresholdExceeded
  · WatchdogTimeout
  · EStopSignal
  · DisconnectCmd
end note

note bottom of emergencyStop
  <b>REQ-005 satisfied by</b>
  SafetyModule::watchdogPeriod
  ≤ 100 ms
end note

@enduml
